%U A399500 11,12,13,14,15,16,6,7,8,9,10,11,13,14,15,16,17,18
%N A399500 Triangle read by rows: row n gives the n consecutive integers centered at n, excluding n if n is even.
%C A399500 This sequence concatenates, row by row, the elements of the centered almost-consecutive sets R(n). Row n has length n. The sets R(n) are defined as follows: for odd n, R(n) = {m+1,...,3m+1} (where n=2m+1); for even n, R(n) = {m,...,2m-1} U {2m+1,...,3m} (where n=2m). The sum of each row is n^2. This is the base sequence for the sets R(n) family; other sequences such as A398929 (frequency function f(x)), A398933 (partial sums of f(x)), A399262 (union of R_3(n)), and A399490 (sum of squares of R(n)) are derived from this construction.
%C A399500 If n is odd, n = 2m+1: row n = {m+1, ..., 3m+1}.
%C A399500 If n is even, n = 2m: row n = {m, ..., 2m-1} U {2m+1, ..., 3m}.
%H A399500 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A399500/b399500.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11325</a> (rows 1..150 of triangle, flattened).
%e A399500 Triangle begins:
%e A399500   n=1: 1
%e A399500   n=2: 1, 3
%e A399500   n=3: 2, 3, 4
%e A399500   n=4: 2, 3, 5, 6
%e A399500   n=5: 3, 4, 5, 6, 7
%e A399500   n=6: 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9
%t A399500 A399500row[n_] := If[OddQ[n], Range @@ ({1, n} + (n-1)/2), Drop[Range[n/2, 3*n/2], {n/2 + 1}]];
%t A399500 Array[A399500row, 15] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Sep 08 2026 *)
%o A399500 (Python)
%o A399500 def R(n):
%o A399500     m = n // 2
%o A399500     if n % 2 == 1:
%o A399500         return list(range(m + 1, 3*m + 2))
%o A399500     else:
%o A399500         return list(range(m, 2*m)) + list(range(2*m + 1, 3*m + 1))
%o A399500 # Print first 10 rows
%o A399500 for n in range(1, 11):
%o A399500     print(R(n))
%Y A399500 Cf. A008619 (1st column), A032766 (right diagonal), A399490.
%Y A399500 Cf. A398929, A398933, A399262.
